WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.422
Safe handling starts with restraint.

2
00:00:02.422 --> 00:00:08.024
Unknown removable media should not be casually connected to a production workstation.

3
00:00:08.024 --> 00:00:23.314
Connecting it directly can alter file system state, update access timestamps, create host artifacts, trigger automatic behavior, expose the workstation to malware risk, or change the evidence in ways that are difficult to explain later.

4
00:00:23.314 --> 00:00:27.023
The first action should be documentation, not curiosity.

5
00:00:27.023 --> 00:00:34.820
A write blocker, at a high level, is used to reduce the chance that evidence media is modified during acquisition or review.

6
00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:43.449
Hardware and software approaches vary, and the right choice depends on media type, tool availability, policy, and case requirements.

7
00:00:43.449 --> 00:00:51.322
Whatever method is used, investigators should document how write protection was applied and any limitations that remain.

8
00:00:51.322 --> 00:00:56.999
Forensic imaging creates a preserved copy of media or logical evidence for examination.

9
00:00:56.999 --> 00:01:01.238
Working from an image or verified copy helps protect the original.

10
00:01:01.238 --> 00:01:07.218
Hashing supports integrity verification by producing a value that can be compared over time.

11
00:01:07.218 --> 00:01:15.393
Hashes do not make evidence true or complete, but they help show whether a file, image, or evidence set changed after collection.

12
00:01:15.393 --> 00:01:21.070
Chain of custody records who handled the evidence, when, why, and under what conditions.

13
00:01:21.070 --> 00:01:28.867
The record should include receipt, storage, imaging, transfer, examination, and any material change in evidence state.

14
00:01:28.867 --> 00:01:39.162
Photographs, labels, packaging notes, device condition, capacity, markings, and connection details all help future reviewers understand what was examined.

15
00:01:39.162 --> 00:01:44.763
Preserving original media and working from verified copies is a practical discipline.

16
00:01:44.763 --> 00:01:52.106
It reduces accidental modification, supports repeatable review, and helps separate acquisition from analysis.

17
00:01:52.106 --> 00:02:02.703
The best handling procedures are boring in the right way: careful, documented, minimal, and designed so another qualified person can understand and repeat the work.
